e the fixed 6x5s loop with an env-tunable exponential-backoff budget ... 195s worst case' to cover 'Jira Cloud's Lucene-index eventual-consistency lag' — a polling approach, with no mention of reconcileIssues.","Atlassian Jira Cloud REST API docs (developer.atlassian.com/cloud/jira/platform/rest/v3/api-group-issue-search): 'Recent updates might not be immediately visible in the returned search results. If you need read-after-write consistency, you can utilize the reconcileIssues parameter to ensure stronger consistency assurances.' — the exact problem §1 describes.","Third-party integration prior art (port-labs/ocean, per DeepWiki) adopts 'POST /rest/api/3/search/jql with reconcileIssues parameter to avoid Jira search index lag.'","Codebase already POSTs to the reconcileIssues-capable endpoint: acli_graph.py:299/388/471 issue `POST /rest/api/3/search/jql`; the probe's own search path (access_check.py:179 -> acli.py:445 `jira workitem search`) currently routes through the acli CLI, so the plan should at least establish whether that path can carry reconcileIssues or justify polling over it."],"finding":"The plan's §1 index-lag remedy (a longer exponential-backoff polling loop, up to ~195s) reinvents a solution to a problem Atlassian documents a purpose-built API remedy for — the `reconcileIssues` parameter on POST /rest/api/3/search/jql — without considering that prior art.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3de30a5a40217c9b","impact":0.33,"is_primary":null,"location":"§1 — Harden the search-index wait (access_check.py); Problem statement","norm_id":"n0f567ce9fef092fc","priority":0.2063,"reason":"default-advisory","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A dispatched live run where index lag still exceeds even the new 195s budget — a reconcileIssues-based read would be deterministic where a longer poll only widens the flake window.","Reviewers/maintainers asking why the probe sleeps up to ~3.25 minutes instead of using the documented consistency parameter."],"severit